When using the -c option (CSV output), every field will be printed regardless of the format string.

.SH EACCT CSV OUTPUT FIELDS
When
.B eacct
is used with the
.B \-c
option, output is written in CSV format.  When
.B \-c
is combined with
.B \-l
or
.B \-r ,
the CSV file contains the full set of metrics stored in the EAR database.

The following fields may appear in CSV output:

.TP
.B JOBID
The job ID.

.TP
.B STEPID
The step ID.

.TP
.B APPID
The EARAM application ID used to identify the workload. This value is useful
to distinguish different applications executed in a workflow within the same
job step.

.TP
.B USERID
The user name of the user who executed the job.

.TP
.B GROUPID
The group name of the user who executed the job.

.TP
.B ACCOUNTID
The account name of the user who executed the job.

.TP
.B JOBNAME
The job name, or the executable name if no job name was provided.

.TP
.B ENERGY_TAG
The energy tag used if the user set one for the job step.

.TP
.B JOB_START_TIME
Unix epoch timestamp, in seconds, when the job step started.

.TP
.B JOB_END_TIME
Unix epoch timestamp, in seconds, when the job step ended.

.TP
.B JOB_EARL_START_TIME
Unix epoch timestamp, in seconds, when EARAM started monitoring the job step;
that is, the application start time.

.TP
.B JOB_EARL_END_TIME
Unix epoch timestamp, in seconds, when EARAM ended monitoring the job step;
that is, the application end time.

.TP
.B POLICY
Energy optimization policy name used by EARAM.
.B MO
means monitoring-only.

.TP
.B POLICY_TH
The policy threshold used by the EARAM optimization policy.

.TP
.B JOB_NPROCS
The number of processes involved in the application.

.TP
.B JOB_TYPE
The job type.

.TP
.B JOB_DEF_FREQ
The default frequency at which the job started.

.TP
.B EARL_ENABLED
Indicates whether the job step ran with EARL enabled. This field is deprecated.

.TP
.B EAR_LEARNING
Indicates whether the application was run in the learning phase.

.TP
.B NODENAME
The node name to which the rest of the row information belongs.

.TP
.B AVG_CPUFREQ_KHZ
Average CPU frequency of the job step executed on the node, expressed in kHz.
This value is computed by EARAM.

.TP
.B AVG_IMCFREQ_KHZ
Average uncore frequency of the job step executed on the node, expressed in
kHz. On AMD sockets, this is the default data fabric frequency. This value is
computed by EARAM.

.TP
.B DEF_FREQ_KHZ
The default frequency of the job step executed on the node, expressed in kHz.
This value corresponds to the default frequency that the EAR Library sets at
the beginning of the execution, and has the same value as
.BR JOB_DEF_FREQ .

.TP
.B TIME_SEC
Execution time period, in seconds, covered by the application metrics reported
by EARAM.

.TP
.B CPI
CPU cycles per instruction. This is a hint for CPU-bound or memory-bound
classification.

.TP
.B TPI
Memory transactions per instruction. This is a hint for CPU-bound or
memory-bound classification.

.TP
.B MEM_GBS
CPU main-memory bandwidth, in GB/s. This is a hint for CPU-bound or
memory-bound classification.

.TP
.B IO_MBS
I/O read and write throughput, in MB/s.

.TP
.B PERC_MPI
Percentage of
.B TIME_SEC
spent in MPI calls.

.TP
.B DC_NODE_POWER_W
Average node power over the time period, in watts. This value differs from
.B NODEMGR_DC_NODE_POWER_W
because it is computed and reported by EARAM.

.TP
.B DRAM_POWER_W
Average DRAM power over the time period, in watts. This field is not available
on AMD sockets. This value differs from
.B NODEMGR_DRAM_POWER_W
because it is computed and reported by EARAM.

.TP
.B PCK_POWER_W
Average RAPL package power over the time period, in watts. This value shows the
aggregated power of all sockets in a package. This value differs from
.B NODEMGR_PCK_POWER_W
because it is computed and reported by EARAM.

.TP
.B CYCLES
Total number of cycles retrieved during the time period.

.TP
.B INSTRUCTIONS
Total number of instructions retrieved during the time period.

.TP
.B CPU_GFLOPS
Total number of CPU giga-floating-point operations per second during the time
period.

.TP
.B CPU_UTIL
CPU time of the application.

.TP
.B L1_MISSES
Total number of L1 cache misses during the time period.

.TP
.B L2_MISSES
Total number of L2 cache misses during the time period.

.TP
.B L3_MISSES
Total number of L3 or LLC cache misses during the time period.

.TP
.B SPOPS_SINGLE
Total number of single-precision 64-bit floating-point operations.

.TP
.B SPOPS_128
Total number of single-precision 128-bit floating-point operations.

.TP
.B SPOPS_256
Total number of single-precision 256-bit floating-point operations.

.TP
.B SPOPS_512
Total number of single-precision 512-bit floating-point operations.

.TP
.B DPOPS_SINGLE
Total number of double-precision 64-bit floating-point operations.

.TP
.B DPOPS_128
Total number of double-precision 128-bit floating-point operations.

.TP
.B DPOPS_256
Total number of double-precision 256-bit floating-point operations.

.TP
.B DPOPS_512
Total number of double-precision 512-bit floating-point operations.

.TP
.B NODEMGR_DC_NODE_POWER_W
Average node power over the time period, in watts. This value differs from
.B DC_NODE_POWER_W
because it is computed and reported by the Node Manager, EARD, independently of
whether EARAM was enabled.

.TP
.B NODEMGR_DRAM_POWER_W
Average DRAM power over the time period, in watts. This field is not available
on AMD sockets. This value differs from
.B DRAM_POWER_W
because it is computed and reported by the Node Manager, EARD, independently of
whether EARAM was enabled.

.TP
.B NODEMGR_PCK_POWER_W
Average RAPL package power over the time period, in watts. This value shows the
aggregated power of all sockets in a package. This value differs from
.B PCK_POWER_W
because it is computed and reported by the Node Manager, EARD, independently of
whether EARAM was enabled.

.TP
.B NODEMGR_MAX_DC_POWER_W
The peak DC node power computed by the Node Manager.

.TP
.B NODEMGR_MIN_DC_POWER_W
The minimum DC node power computed by the Node Manager.

.TP
.B NODEMGR_TIME_SEC
Execution time period, in seconds, covered by the job-step metrics reported by
the Node Manager.

.TP
.B NODEMGR_AVG_CPUFREQ_KHZ
Average CPU frequency computed by the Node Manager during the job-step
execution time.

.TP
.B NODEMGR_DEF_FREQ_KHZ
Default frequency set by the Node Manager when the job step began.

.SS GPU CSV fields
If EAR is installed in a cluster with GPU partitions, the following additional
CSV fields may be present. In fields named
.BR GPUx_* ,
.B x
identifies the GPU index.

.TP
.B GPUx_POWER_W
Average power of GPU
.BR x ,
in watts.

.TP
.B GPUx_FREQ_KHZ
Average frequency of GPU
.BR x ,
in kHz.

.TP
.B GPUx_MEM_FREQ_KHZ
Average memory frequency of GPU
.BR x ,
in kHz.

.TP
.B GPUx_UTIL_PERC
Average utilization percentage of GPU
.BR x .

.TP
.B GPUx_MEM_UTIL_PERC
Average memory-utilization percentage of GPU
.BR x .

.TP
.B GPUx_GFLOPS
GFLOPS reported for GPU
.BR x .

.TP
.B GPUx_TEMP
Average temperature of GPU
.BR x .

.TP
.B GPUx_MEMTEMP
Average memory temperature of GPU
.BR x .

.TP
.B GPUi_GR_ENGINE_ACTIVE
Graphics-engine activity.

.TP
.B GPUi_SM_ACTIVE
SM activity.

.TP
.B GPUi_SM_OCCUPANCY
SM occupancy.

.TP
.B GPUi_TENSOR_ACTIVE
Tensor activity.

.TP
.B GPUi_DRAM_ACTIVE
Memory-bandwidth utilization.

.TP
.B GPUi_FP64_ACTIVE
FP64 engine activity.

.TP
.B GPUi_FP32_ACTIVE
FP32 engine activity.

.TP
.B GPUi_FP16_ACTIVE
FP16 engine activity.

.TP
.B GPUi_PCIE_TX_BYTES
PCIe bandwidth for writes.

.TP
.B GPUi_PCIE_RX_BYTES
PCIe bandwidth for reads.

.TP
.B GPUi_NVLINK_TX_BYTES
NVLink bandwidth for writes.

.TP
.B GPUi_NVLINK_RX_BYTES
NVLink bandwidth for reads.




